<article class="env-lemma" id="A2BB38">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/A2BB38">Lemma <span data-tag="A2BB38">6.5.3.5</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-topos, and let $U$ be an $\infty $-connective object of $\calX $. Let $U_{\bullet }$ be the constant simplicial object with value $U$. Then $U_{\bullet }$ is a hypercovering of $\calX $. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Lemma <a href="/tag/05528B" data-tag="05528B">6.5.3.4</a>, we can reduce to the case where $\calX $ is hypercomplete. Then $U \simeq 1_{\calX }$, so that $U_{\bullet }$ is equivalent to the constant functor with value $1_{\calX }$, and is therefore a final object of $\calX _{\Delta }$. For each $n \geq 0$, the coskeleton functor $\cosk _{n-1}$ preserves small limits, so $\cosk _{n-1} U_{\bullet }$ is also a final object of $U_{\bullet }$. It follows that the unit map $U_{\bullet } \rightarrow \cosk _{n-1} U_{\bullet }$ is an equivalence. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>